.TH ESDM\-EXTRACTLSB 8 "2026-08-05" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-extractlsb \- extract the significant bits of raw noise samples
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-extractlsb
.I INPUTFILE OUTFILE MAXEVENTS MASK
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-extractlsb
turns the decimal samples produced by
.BR esdm\-getrawentropy (8)
or
.BR esdm\-ebpf\-collect (8)
into the binary byte stream the NIST SP800\-90B entropy assessment tools
expect. For every input line it selects the bits named by
.I MASK
from the 64 bit sample, packs them down into one byte and writes that byte.
.PP
The mask is what makes the assessment meaningful: the timing entropy of these
sources sits in the low\-order bits, so
.B FF
\- the low 8 \- is the usual choice, and the one the assessment scripts use.
.PP
This tool is built with the meson option
.BR validation\-helpers .
It is for measurement and validation only.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I INPUTFILE
File of decimal samples, one per line.
.TP
.I OUTFILE
Binary output file, one byte per input sample. It must not exist \- an existing
file is not overwritten.
.TP
.I MAXEVENTS
Stop after this many input samples.
.TP
.I MASK
Up to 16 hexadecimal digits naming the bits to keep. At most 8 bits may be
set, since the SP800\-90B tools assess at most 8 bits per sample.
.SH OUTPUT
Besides the binary file, a summary is printed:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
the number of samples processed, the mask and how many bits it selects,
.IP \(bu 2
the bits that were constant 0 across every sample, and
.IP \(bu 2
the bits that were constant 1 across every sample.
.RE
.PP
The two constant\-bit lines are worth reading. A bit that never changes carries
no entropy, so a mask selecting such bits inflates the sample count without
adding signal, and a stream whose selected bits are largely constant indicates
a clock source too coarse for the source to be credited in this environment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, and 1 on a malformed mask, a mask selecting more than 8
bits, or an I/O error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Keep the low 8 bits of a million samples and run the non\-IID estimator:
.PP
.RS
.nf
esdm\-extractlsb /tmp/data\-0001.out /tmp/data\-0001.extracted.out 1000000 FF
ea_non_iid /tmp/data\-0001.extracted.out 8
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
This tool is taken from the LRNG project and adapted, see
.I https://github.com/smuellerDD/lrng/tree/master/test/sp80090b
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-getrawentropy (8),
.BR esdm\-ebpf\-collect (8),
.BR esdm\-server (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephan Mueller <smueller@chronox.de>
